WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:10.880
Welcome to the Council, on a European summit
day. The 27 heads of state and government

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:17.300
meet regularly here in Brussels. Today, they
have very serious matters to discuss: the

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:24.300
disaster in Japan, the crisis in Libya and
the Euro.

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:31.610
We are going to discuss the situation in Japan,
the situation of the nuclear plant in Fukushima

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:41.710
has showed me as a German Chancellor that
we cannot continue to act as before.

00:00:46.039 --> 00:00:50.449
This is an important European Council, it
is important that the countries of Europe

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:54.390
show political will, ambition and unity.

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:59.179
The changes in a number of Arab countries
are of a historic dimension.

00:00:59.179 --> 00:01:06.179
We must make sure we are all on the same page,
to define a clear line so that our action

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:09.800
can be in concert with that of the international
community.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:16.800
The challenge now is that Europe as a whole
sends a very strong and convincing message

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:24.970
to the international markets that it is supporting
a stable euro and all Eurozone countries.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:34.170
The 27 EU leaders are convened by the permanent
President of the European Council, Herman

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:37.180
Van Rompuy.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:44.180
The European Council is comprised of the heads
of state and government of the 27 EU Member

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:51.530
States. I chair meetings of the European Council,
of which there are at least 4 each year, and

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:58.600
in practice 6 or 7. The European Council gives
the European Union its main impetus by providing

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:03.300
the broad lines and priorities for EU policies.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:10.300
All European citizens are directly affected
by what is discussed around this table.

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:19.470
It is here that, at the start of the meeting,
the heads of state and government greet each

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:24.810
other. But they are not the only ones who
use this room… Other meetings of ministers

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:29.370
and meetings of the Council are also held
here, such as the Councils of Ministers of

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:36.060
Agriculture, Transport, the Environment and
Foreign Affairs, and each time, you have the

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:41.810
27 delegations plus the Presidency and the
Commission in attendance.

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:48.810
The Council is the main decision-making body,
although it does increasingly share this role

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:56.380
with the European Parliament. What is specific
to the Council is that here the Member States

00:02:56.380 --> 00:03:01.350
cooperate and negotiate on a daily basis.

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:06.380
...This takes place at all levels: at the
highest level with the European Council, at

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:10.630
ministerial level with the Council of Ministers,
at the level of the ambassadors and the permanent

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:15.300
representatives committee, COREPER, and at
base level, i.e. that of the working groups

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:20.090
comprising national civil servants."

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:25.060
The ministers examine the Commission’s legislative
proposals and share the decisions with the

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:31.849
European Parliament in a large number of areas.
For all legislative work, the Ministers deliberate

00:03:31.849 --> 00:03:37.730
in public, and their debates can be followed
live online.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:42.900
I think it's right or proper that our emphasis
should be on renewable technologies and energy

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:46.060
efficiency technologies particularly.

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:50.590
The Ministers representing the Member States
are committed by the decisions that they take

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:51.010
together.

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:58.010
Good morning! Today we have a fisheries agenda,
we have to fix the quotas during the day,

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.930
and tomorrow we have to take action to prevent
illegal logging…

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:05.180
Today, the 27 ministers of economic affairs
have taken an important decision to stimulate

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:10.209
innovation in Europe: they have given the
greenlight to a simplified European patent

00:04:10.209 --> 00:04:15.450
framework. This will considerably alleviate
administrative burdens on inventors.

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:22.450
The Hungarian Presidency is convinced that
greater cooperation on the European patent

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:29.900
will directly benefit 500 million Europeans
and all the businesses of Europeans, irrespective

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:33.400
of their nations

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:38.750
Once a month, the foreign ministers meet at
the Concil under the presidency of High Representative

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:39.580
Catherine Ashton.

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:46.580
The critical thing at the moment is the decision
that was taken under UN resolution 1973 to

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:54.130
do everything we can to support the people
on the ground, the people in Libya

00:04:54.130 --> 00:05:01.130
The High Representative is also in charge
of the Union's external aid.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:07.500
Europe can launch missions to manage crises
in troubled regions. At the moment, these

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:13.270
European ships are fighting piracy off the
coast of Somalia, and European soldiers are

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:16.940
training Somali troops to help restore order
in their country.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:23.940
Europe's citizens are at the heart of the
Council's concerns. For the Ministers of Justice

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:29.090
and Home Affairs, that means helping citizens
to better enjoy one of the great advantages

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:36.090
of the European Union: freedom of movement.
As a recent popular movie reminds us; today,

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:43.250
thanks to Europe, there's no longer any need
to say: "nothing to declare".

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:47.860
It reminds me of when we were young. When
we crossed the border there was a customs

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:53.310
post. You had to declare any goods, show your
passport. When we were with our parents, there

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:58.070
was even some tension, when we went to France,
or the Netherlands, or Luxembourg, it was

00:05:58.070 --> 00:06:05.070
a kind of adventure, we really had the impression
that we were leaving our country. Today, we're

00:06:06.509 --> 00:06:10.860
in Europe, there are no more borders, you
just cross the border without realising it.

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:14.770
Psychologically speaking it's a completely
different world.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:21.770
Now, from 7 countries which had decided to
abolish border controls, we now have 25…

00:06:22.759 --> 00:06:26.250
This is an extension of the space of freedom
in Europe

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:33.250
Return to the European Council in March 2011.
A big decision has just been taken: The pact

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:41.009
for the Eurozone

00:06:41.009 --> 00:06:48.009
We adopted the Euro Plus Pact. It will provide
a new quality of economic coordination.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:53.080
We have put in place the economic government
of Europe.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:58.100
I welcome the steps that the Eurozone has
taken today

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:03.580
We now have the pact for the Euro, in addition
to the 17 Euro member states, we have six

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:06.539
states in support. I think that very encouraging.

00:07:06.539 --> 00:07:13.539
I think we have no other choice but to focus
on the economy; if we want to be taken seriously

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:20.210
in the world, we need to be strong economically.
If we want to protect our social model, we

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:27.210
need a strong economy in order to finance
it. In reality, our task is simple: greater

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:32.599
economic strength, so that we can also defend
our values in the world more effectively.

